#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# factor_terms

#% text
# `factor_terms(p)` pulls out the numerical content of p: the gcd of its integer coefficients.

#% text
# `factor_terms(p, x)` also pulls out the factors free of x (the gcd of the coefficients of the powers of x); `factor_terms(p, [x1, x2, ...])` does so for each variable in turn.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Lists and the sides of comparisons are handled element-wise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
factor_terms(3 + 6*x + 3*x^2)
#% output
#= 3*(1 + 2*x + x^2)

#% cell
factor_terms(3 + 3*a + 6*a*x + 6*x + 12*a*x^2 + 12*x^2, x)
#% output
#= 3*(1 + a)*(1 + 2*x + 4*x^2)

#% cell
factor_terms(7*x + (14*y + 21)/z)
#% output
#= 7*(x + 3/z + 2*y/z)

#% cell
factor_terms(-6*y - 6*a*y + 2*x^2*y + 2*a*x^2*y + 4*a*y^2 + 4*a^2*y^2, [x, y])
#% output
#= 2*y*(1 + a)*(-3 + 2*a*y + x^2)

#% text
# `modulus: m` reduces the coefficients modulo `m` and pulls out the leading coefficient when it is invertible:

#% cell
factor_terms(5*x^2 + 2, modulus: 3)
#% output
#= 2*(1 + x^2)

#% cell
factor_terms(3*x + 10, modulus: 7)
#% output
#= 3*(1 + x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `factor`, `factor_list`, `collect`
